summary: MLS permissive boot AVC/SELINUX_ERR check (COPR)
description: |
    Simple first-step plan: install COPR selinux-policy-mls, switch to MLS
    with prepare_for_mls (permissive, fixfiles -F onboot, one reboot), stay
    permissive, then FAIL if ausearch finds AVC/USER_AVC/SELINUX_ERR since
    boot, PASS if none.

    Does not switch to enforcing and does not run Fedora tier1 tests.
    See /tmt/mls-copr-testsuite for the enforcing + tier1 follow-up.

    Env: COPR_REPO (required); optional COPR_SELINUX_POLICY_MLS_NVR.

environment:
  MLS_STAY_PERMISSIVE: "1"

prepare:
  - name: COPR MLS permissive switch
    how: shell
    script: $TMT_TREE/tmt/mls-copr-prepare.sh

discover:
  - name: permissive-avc
    how: shell
    tests:
      - name: /permissive-avc/check
        duration: 10m
        require:
          - audit
        test: $TMT_TREE/tmt/mls-copr-permissive-avc-check.sh

execute:
  how: tmt
